ath d="M164,172 V50.72 q0,-4 4,-4 h32 q4,0 4,4 V172 Z"></path><text class="hm-chart__val" x="184" y="38.72" text-anchor="middle">$2.61M</text><text class="hm-chart__tick" x="184" y="190" text-anchor="middle">Jun</text></g><g class="hm-chart__bar"><title>Jul: $2.58M</title><rect class="hm-chart__hit" x="220" y="8" width="72" height="184"></rect><path d="M236,172 V52.16 q0,-4 4,-4 h32 q4,0 4,4 V172 Z"></path><text class="hm-chart__val" x="256" y="40.16" text-anchor="middle">$2.58M</text><text class="hm-chart__tick" x="256" y="190" text-anchor="middle">Jul</text></g><g class="hm-chart__bar"><title>Aug: $2.52M</title><rect class="hm-chart__hit" x="292" y="8" width="72" height="184"></rect><path d="M308,172 V55.040000000000006 q0,-4 4,-4 h32 q4,0 4,4 V172 Z"></path><text class="hm-chart__val" x="328" y="43.040000000000006" text-anchor="middle">$2.52M</text><text class="hm-chart__tick" x="328" y="190" text-anchor="middle">Aug</text></g><g class="hm-chart__bar is-labelled"><title>Sep: $2.49M</title><rect class="hm-chart__hit" x="364" y="8" width="72" height="184"></rect><path d="M380,172 V56.47999999999999 q0,-4 4,-4 h32 q4,0 4,4 V172 Z"></path><text class="hm-chart__val" x="400" y="44.47999999999999" text-anchor="middle">$2.49M</text><text class="hm-chart__tick" x="400" y="190" text-anchor="middle">Sep</text></g></svg><div class="hm-mock__foot"><span><i class="hm-dot hm-dot--ok" aria-hidden="true"></i> 6 of 6 monthly snapshots certified</span><span>−8.1% in six months</span></div></div></div></article><article class="pf-module pf-module--flip" id="reconciliation"><div class="pf-module__copy" data-reveal="true"><p class="pf-module__eyebrow"><span>02</span>Automation &amp; data integrity</p><h2>The work of a finance department, done every day.</h2><p class="pf-module__lede">Processor, client system, CRM and books reconciled continuously. Migrations between incompatible systems reconciled record by record. Anything that can&#x27;t be tied is counted and queued for a person.</p><dl class="pf-caps"><div><dt>Ranked match suggestions</dt><dd>Unmatched payments get the five most likely clients by name similarity, amount and timing. A person confirms. Nothing is matched on a guess.</dd></div><div><dt>Duplicates and orphans healed</dt><dd>Duplicate client records merged into one survivor with every related table repointed. Contracts with no client re-linked or given one.</dd></div><div><dt>Booked once, audited always</dt><dd>Idempotency guards stop a payment being booked twice on webhook retries. Every merge, link and reclassification is written to an audit table and reversible.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="pf-module__visual hm-panel__visual" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="120"><div class="hm-mock"><div class="hm-mock__head"><span>Daily checks</span><span class="hm-example">Example data</span></div><ul class="hm-checks"><li><span class="hm-checks__name">Monthly receivables snapshot</span><span class="hm-chip hm-chip--ok">Certified</span><span class="hm-checks__meta">Captured on the 1st · 12-month trend</span></li><li><span class="hm-checks__name">Processor to client system</span><span class="hm-chip hm-chip--ok">Healthy</span><span class="hm-checks__meta">2,013 matched · 759 queued for a person</span></li><li class="is-flagged"><span class="hm-checks__name">Contracts marked paid with no payments</span><span class="hm-chip hm-chip--warn">Flagged</span><span class="hm-checks__meta">428 found with ~4% collected · reclassified, reversible</span></li><li><span class="hm-checks__name">Duplicate and orphan clients</span><span class="hm-chip hm-chip--ok">Healthy</span><span class="hm-checks__meta">561 contracts re-linked · 89 duplicates merged</span></li><li><span class="hm-checks__name">Double-booking guard</span><span class="hm-chip hm-chip--ok">Healthy</span><span class="hm-checks__meta">A retried payment can&#x27;t be booked twice</span></li></ul></div></div></article><article class="pf-module" id="collections"><div class="pf-module__copy" data-reveal="true"><p class="pf-module__eyebrow"><span>03</span>Connect</p><h2>Rebuild the connection between your firm and the clients who owe it.</h2><p class="pf-module__lede">A prioritized queue, automated email and SMS to the right client lists, and a record of every message, promise and reply. A person steps in only when the client needs one.</p><dl class="pf-caps"><div><dt>Queue intelligence</dt><dd>Accounts ranked by balance, aging and last contact, built from reconciled balances. Consult-only records, import noise and abandoned contracts stay out by default.</dd></div><div><dt>Automated messaging, in your voice</dt><dd>Missed installment, failed card, balance due, plan complete: each list gets its own email and SMS sequence, sent from your firm, logged on the account, and stopped the moment a payment lands.</dd></div><div><dt>Commitments and hardship</dt><dd>Promises to pay carry a date and amount and get followed up automatically. Hardship requests are a workflow, not a sticky note.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="pf-module__visual hm-panel__visual" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="120"><div class="hm-mock hm-mock--thread"><div class="hm-mock__head"><span>Ana Morales · Payment plan</span><span class="hm-example">Example data</span></div><ol class="hm-thread"><li class="hm-msg hm-msg--out"><span class="hm-msg__meta">Text · 9:14 AM · Delivered</span>Hi Ana, it&#x27;s the billing team at Morgan &amp; Hale. The card on your payment plan didn&#x27;t go through. You can update it here in about a minute: <u>pay.morganhale.com/u/8F2K</u></li><li class="hm-msg hm-msg--in"><span class="hm-msg__meta">Reply · 9:31 AM</span>Done, sorry about that. Can I catch up on the 15th?</li><li class="hm-event"><i class="hm-dot hm-dot--ok" aria-hidden="true"></i> Card updated · promise logged: $1,050 on Oct 15</li></ol></div></div></article><article class="pf-module pf-module--flip" id="accountability"><div class="pf-module__copy" data-reveal="true"><p class="pf-module__eyebrow"><span>04</span>Accountability</p><h2>Every team member, every outreach, every dollar, every day.</h2><p class="pf-module__lede">Scorecards for billing, client relations and intake, built from the full activity log and certified per person.</p><dl class="pf-caps"><div><dt>Monthly scorecards</dt><dd>Outreach, dollars collected, average per contact, commission, collection rate, contacts per day and connected per day, per team member.</dd></div><div><dt>Outcomes and origins</dt><dd>Where collected dollars came from (AR list, email sequence, SMS, follow-up, transfer, service-team request) and how each contact ended, with dirty labels normalized.</dd></div><div><dt>Today, not last month</dt><dd>A date-stamped row per team member for the current day, and new-client contact counts by day of week.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="pf-module__visual hm-panel__visual" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="120"><div class="hm-mock pf-screens"><div class="hm-mock__head"><span>Accountability</span><span class="hm-example">Screens</span></div><ul><li class="is-on"><span>Team Performance</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Collections KPI</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Outcome Distribution</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Origin breakdown</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Coverage tracking</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li></ul></div></div></article><article class="pf-module" id="escalations"><div class="pf-module__copy" data-reveal="true"><p class="pf-module__eyebrow"><span>05</span>Unique escalations &amp; internal connection</p><h2>Hand-offs with a queue, a priority and an owner.</h2><p class="pf-module__lede">Billing, service teams, intake and management look at the same record. An escalation has a status that has to be closed.</p><dl class="pf-caps"><div><dt>Seven hand-off queues</dt><dd>Service teams, compliance, customer care, management, sales, billing ops and a custom queue, each with its own inbox and the live roster as assignees.</dd></div><div><dt>Context travels with it</dt><dd>Source (client reply, service-team request, refund follow-up, compliance review), priority, notes and the client&#x27;s ledger, all on the escalation.</dd></div><div><dt>Deadlines in view</dt><dd>Service and contract deadlines appear on the client record and in a firm-wide panel, so collections never collides with a commitment the firm has made.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="pf-module__visual hm-panel__visual" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="120"><div class="hm-mock"><div class="hm-mock__head"><span>Escalation · Service team inbox</span><span class="hm-example">Example data</span></div><div class="hm-esc"><div class="hm-esc__top"><span class="hm-chip hm-chip--warn">High priority</span><span class="hm-esc__age">Opened 2h ago · due today</span></div><p class="hm-esc__title">Client asks to move this month&#x27;s installment to the 30th</p><dl><div><dt>Client</dt><dd>Ana Morales · Payment plan</dd></div><div><dt>Source</dt><dd>Client reply to a text</dd></div><div><dt>From</dt><dd>Billing team</dd></div><div><dt>Owner</dt><dd>Service team · case lead</dd></div></dl><div class="hm-esc__trail"><span><i class="hm-dot hm-dot--ok" aria-hidden="true"></i> Ledger attached</span><span><i class="hm-dot hm-dot--ok" aria-hidden="true"></i> Deadline watch: no conflict</span></div></div></div></div></article><article class="pf-module pf-module--flip" id="products"><div class="pf-module__copy" data-reveal="true"><p class="pf-module__eyebrow"><span>06</span>Products &amp; lifecycle</p><h2>Which products make the money, and when it arrives.</h2><p class="pf-module__lede">Billing by product, contract lifecycle and the service pipeline by stage, so partners can see what to sell more of.</p><dl class="pf-caps"><div><dt>Cash by product</dt><dd>What each product line bills and collects, and how long it takes to do it.</dd></div><div><dt>Contract lifecycle</dt><dd>From signed to current to paid, with abandoned and delinquent contracts classified honestly instead of hidden in ‘Paid’.</dd></div><div><dt>Service pipeline</dt><dd>Active engagements by stage, product mix and twelve months of intakes, next to the money those engagements produce.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="pf-module__visual hm-panel__visual" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="120"><div class="hm-mock pf-screens"><div class="hm-mock__head"><span>Products &amp; lifecycle</span><span class="hm-example">Screens</span></div><ul><li class="is-on"><span>Billing by Product</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Contract Lifecycle</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Contract Progression</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Service Pipeline by Stage</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Product Mix</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Monthly Intakes</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li></ul></div></div></article><article class="pf-module" id="crm"><div class="pf-module__copy" data-reveal="true"><p class="pf-module__eyebrow"><span>07</span>Works with your CRM</p><h2>Compatible with any CRM that exports or has an API.</h2><p class="pf-module__lede">Contact, engagements, ledger, plan and escalations on one screen, with the latest processor payments blended in. Your CRM stays your CRM.</p><dl class="pf-caps"><div><dt>Everything about the client</dt><dd>Contact details, engagements, payment ledger and plan from the client system, plus fresh processor payments with a freshness stamp.</dd></div><div><dt>Leads validated by money</dt><dd>HubSpot deals marked won become active clients only when payment evidence exists. Email segments come from reconciled balances, so the right client gets the right message.</dd></div><div><dt>Take a payment, correctly</dt><dd>Card or ACH, routed to operating or Trust / IOLTA based on what it&#x27;s for, logged as an activity on the account.</dd></div></dl></div><