storical Collections</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li><li><span>Report Builder</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li></ul></div></div></article></div></section></div><section class="section section--light pf-compare" id="compare"><div class="container"><div class="section-head" data-reveal="true"><p class="eyebrow">Compare</p><h2>How LexCollect compares.</h2><p class="lead">Most firms track receivables with a collections tool, a spreadsheet, or both. Here&#x27;s where the difference shows up.</p></div><div class="pf-compare__wrap" data-reveal="true"><table class="pf-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col" class="is-us">LexCollect</th><th scope="col">Collections tool</th><th scope="col">Spreadsheet + report</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Starts from</th><td class="is-us">A reconciled book</td><td>Who owes money</td><td>Whatever was exported</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Reconciles client system, processor, CRM, books and bank</th><td class="is-us yes">Continuously</td><td class="no">No</td><td>Manually, monthly</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Automated email and SMS to reconciled client lists</th><td class="is-us yes">Yes, in your voice</td><td>Dialer</td><td class="no">No</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Separates failed cards from delinquency</th><td class="is-us yes">Yes</td><td class="no">No</td><td class="no">No</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Per-person scorecards from the full activity log</th><td class="is-us yes">Yes, certified</td><td>Contact counts</td><td class="no">No</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Escalations with queues, priorities and inboxes</th><td class="is-us yes">Seven queues</td><td>Notes</td><td class="no">No</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cash by product and contract lifecycle</th><td class="is-us yes">Yes</td><td class="no">No</td><td>If someone builds it</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Trust / IOLTA vs operating routing</th><td class="is-us yes">Yes</td><td class="no">No</td><td class="no">No</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Integrations</th><td class="is-us">Any CRM with export or API · MyCase, Filevine, LawPay, HubSpot, QuickBooks, bank</td><td>Processor</td><td>Exports</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section class="section pf-start" id="start"><div class="container"><div class="section-head" data-reveal="true"><p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p><h2>From first conversation to first certified snapshot.</h2></div><ol class="tl"><li class="tl__item" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="0"><span class="tl__kicker">Step 01</span><h3>Connect your systems</h3><p>We connect your client-management system, payment processor, CRM, accounting and bank data, and pull history.</p></li><li class="tl__item" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="90"><span class="tl__kicker">Step 02</span><h3>Reconcile and configure</h3><p>You get the first reconciled book with the gaps named, and we set roles, roster, queues, message sequences and product lines to match your firm.</p></li><li class="tl__item" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="180"><span class="tl__kicker">Step 03</span><h3>Work the queue</h3><p>Sequences go out to reconciled lists and your team works the clients who need a person. The first month ends with a certified number.</p></li></ol></div></section><section class="section section--deep section--rule"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div data-reveal="true"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Platform FAQ</h2></div><div class="faq"><details open=""><summary><h3>Does LexCollect replace our client-management or accounting software?</h3></summary><div><p>No. LexCollect sits across the systems you already use and reconciles them. Your team keeps working in the same client-management and accounting tools.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>What happens when a payment can&#x27;t be matched automatically?</h3></summary><div><p>It&#x27;s counted, queued and shown with ranked suggestions. A person confirms the match, and the confirmation is recorded. Nothing is matched on a guess and nothing is dropped.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>Who on our team uses it?</h3></summary><div><p>Partners and owners for the certified number and executive insights. Controllers and administrators for management, forecasting and reporting. Billing and client relations for the Connect queue, sequences and commitments. Service teams for the pipeline, deadline watch and their escalation inbox. Access is by role.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>How is it configured for our firm?</h3></summary><div><p>Your team comes from a live roster. Escalation targets are your departments. Message sequences, product lines, outcome labels, origin buckets and aging thresholds are set per firm. Integrations are the ones you already run, and any CRM that exports or has an API can be connected.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>Is LexCollect a collections agency? Do you provide collectors?</h3></summary><div><p>No to both. LexCollect is the accounting department&#x27;s toolkit, delivered as a service: the reconciled book, the queues, the automated email and SMS, the commitments and the record. Your firm keeps the client relationship and decides who is contacted, when and how.</p></div></details></div></div></div></section><section class="cta-band"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Book a call</p><h2>Start with a reconciled book and a connected client list.</h2><p class="lead">We&#x27;ll walk through your systems and show you what LexCollect would find first.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="<?php echo esc_url( lexcollect_booking_url() ); ?>">Book a call <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
